+# Aegis Risk Mitigation Playbook (Operators)
+
+This runbook describes how to use the supplied tools to mitigate the key risks:
+
+1) Hallucination / Adversarial
+ - Run the adversarial CI (.github/workflows/adversarial_factuality.yml) regularly and after model changes.
+ - Review /tmp/adversarial_failures.json and create remediation items.
+ - Tune factuality calibrator and store thresholds in Vault (services/factuality/multimodal_calibrator.py).
+
+2) Key compromise & split custody
+ - Use ops/hsm/initialize_and_test.sh and rotation_ceremony.md for key lifecycle.
+ - Use ops/hsm/kill_switch.sh to disable automated signing/actions immediately if compromise suspected.
+ - Use services/security/split_custody_checker.py + delegation_enforcer.py in orchestrators to require m-of-n approvals.
+
+3) Cost & runaway infra
+ - Enable per-tenant quotas via services/llm/proxy_quota_middleware.py (Redis-backed).
+ - Deploy services/monitoring/token_budget_enforcer.py to alert on budget overruns.
+ - Run services/autoscale/autoscale_guard.py and services/warm_pool/size_monitor.py to guard scale and warm-pool sizing.
+
+4) Legal/Finance exposure
+ - Use delegation manifests and services/policy/delegation_enforcer.py to require approvals for high-risk actions.
+ - Run finance_shadow_multi_month.py and prepare audit binders; use services/finance/prepare_audit_binder.py to create signed binders.
+
+5) Moderation failures
+ - Configure MODERATION_API_URL or provider adapters (services/safety/moderation_openai.py or moderation_aws.py).
+ - Use services/safety/moderation_attest.py to sign moderation manifests and store them in Vault and evidence bucket.
+ - Escalate on 'review' or 'block' via remediation tickets.
+
+6) Continuous improvement
+ - Keep policy CI green (services/policy/expand_and_assert_policy.py).
+ - Schedule periodic rotation ceremonies and DR drills (ops/backup/drill_restore.sh).
